<title>USA: CompuServe international president resigns.</title>
<headline>CompuServe international president resigns.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>CompuServe Inc said on Firday its president of international operations, Steven Stanbrook, is resigning effective early November to become an executive vice president of S.C. Johnson, a consumer products firm.</p>
<p>CompuServe said Jerry Roest, general manager of Europe, and William Truesdell, director of international operations, would now report directly to Denny Matteucci, president of Online Services.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
